# PO Preflight — Git & Team Collaboration Rules

## 1. Branching Strategy
- `main`: Production-ready stable code.
- `dev`: Primary integration branch (default branch for PRs).
- Feature branches: `feat/<feature-name>` (e.g. `feat/fe-orders-queue`, `feat/be-fastapi-gateway`).
- Bugfix branches: `fix/<bug-name>`.

## 2. Commit Message Standards (Conventional Commits)
- `feat:` New feature or capability.
- `fix:` Bug fix.
- `docs:` Documentation updates.
- `refactor:` Code refactoring without behavioral change.
- `test:` Adding or updating tests.
- `chore:` Tooling, configuration, or dependency updates.

## 3. Pull Request Guidelines
- Always link the corresponding GitHub Issue number in the PR description (e.g., `Closes #2`).
- Ensure all automated tests pass before requesting review.
